<!--
    kuna-switchguardmerge: a switch with far outliers (option switchguardmerge).

    Source (x86-64, -O2):
      int two(int x) {
        switch (x) {
        case 0: return f0(x); ... case 6: return f6(x);
        case 100: return f8(x + 1); case 200: return f9(x);
        }
        return -1;
      }

    gcc guards the jump table with x <= 6 and tests 100 and 200 on the
    guard's other side, so the default's case labels split into
    if (a0 <= 6) { switch ... } if (a0 == 100) ...

    Stage: P2/switchnorm, ActionSwitchGuardMerge: the guard is evaluated on
    the outliers and on every case label, the equality chain becomes two more
    cases, and the guard is removed.

    Pass 1 (default) prints one switch with case 100 and case 200; pass 2
    (switchguardmerge off) the guard and the separate tests.
-->
